  "notes": "Scratch slide retune. Not the live profile and not packed. L position gains. Yaw is a 1.5 s raised cosine that finishes 0.9 s before burnout, or as soon as a late pad slide opens. Return speed 2.3 m/s and 11 deg tilt apply only while the stage reference is still more than 2 m away. The 11 deg overshoot holds the chase east of the stick backstop: creep at 0.35 m/s while the arms are still parallel inside the last metre, and brake when the arrival is too fast for the 6 deg cone. Below 0.6 m, Y damping rises to 4.5 only while the body is already south of the pad and still moving south, and the Y tilt cap opens from 5 deg to 9 deg with the cone at 11 deg. Five degrees is already saturated, so more damping alone does not stop the south walk. The pad ease starts on the holding waypoint and does not jump up to the live altitude. A motor that meets a bar fails the flight: the case is the pivot standoff plus the catalog length, with the catalog diameter. Measured CoM kept.",
